---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../../site.config.mjs";
---

<SiteLayout title={`${site.name} — Verified immigration information`} description={site.description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Verified immigration information</p>
    <h1>Understand the rules.<br />Then choose a path.</h1>
    <p class="lede">{site.description} We start with official sources and build information that is searchable, comparable, and traceable.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="/countries">Browse countries</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/match">Check your options</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/about">How we review information</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="start-heading" class="section-block">
    <h2 id="start-heading">How the information is organized</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card"><p class="step">01</p><h2>Browse countries</h2><p>Find the responsible authority, official entry point, and current coverage status.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="step">02</p><h2>Review programs</h2><p>Understand eligibility, fees, timing, family options, and long-term pathways through normalized fields.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><p class="step">03</p><h2>Check options</h2><p>Use transparent rules to identify possible matches, clear barriers, and questions that still require confirmation.</p><p><a href="/match">Try the Canada pre-screen</a></p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <aside class="notice home-notice">
    <h2>Reviewed coverage across 33 countries</h2>
    <p>Compare 71 reviewed immigration and work-residence pathways with links to official government sources. Coverage continues to expand, and requirements should always be reconfirmed before acting.</p>
  </aside>
</SiteLayout>
